\begin{align*}
\begin{vmatrix}
1 & k & -1 \\
k & -1 & -1 \\
1 & 1 & -k
\end{vmatrix} &= 1 \begin{vmatrix} -1 & -1 \\ 1 & -k \end{vmatrix} - k \begin{vmatrix} k & -1 \\ 1 & -k \end{vmatrix} - 1 \begin{vmatrix} k & -1 \\ 1 & 1 \end{vmatrix} \\
&= 1(k + 1) - k(-k - 1) - 1(k + 1) \\
&= k^2 + 2k
\end{align*}

Setting the determinant equal to zero, we get:

\begin{align*}
k^2 + 2k &= 0 \\
k(k + 2) &= 0
\end{align*}

